WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.930
We all have that one toy from our childhood
we held near and dear to our hearts.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:10.690
From stuffed bears to action figures, every
child has something meaningful to them that

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.690
they clung to.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:17.360
It may have been a gift from a parent or grandparent,
or maybe it was an old family memento passed

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.770
down from generation to generation.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:24.590
Regardless, those of us who had these toys
became extremely connected to them physically

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.470
and emotionally.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:31.039
Perhaps you talked to this toy like it was
your friend, or clung to it during nights

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:34.110
where it was storming in order to comfort
yourself.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:39.620
What if these toys were getting the same feelings
back towards us and we didn’t realize it?

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.190
It's a question that only those in the universe
of the SCP Foundation could find a proper

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.930
answer to.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:49.989
SCP-174 - Ventriloquist’s Dummy.

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:53.200
It was a normal day for SCP-174 and its owner.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.560
Mary, a nine-year-old girl, has a pretty ordinary
existence for a girl her age.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.810
A room decorated in pink and obvious fashion.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:06.439
Her school books and art supplies sat on her
little desk in the corner and all of her dolls

00:01:06.439 --> 00:01:09.580
and toys neatly sat on the shelves on the
wall.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.730
She wakes up around 8 o'clock for her third-grade
classes at the nearby elementary school, where

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.740
she is driven to by her father every day.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:24.270
She gets dressed quickly in her school uniform,
SCP-174 remembers a long blue skirt, white

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.560
button-up shirt, and flat, black shoes.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:33.490
This was routine, SCP-174 watched her every
day to the point it became part of it’s

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.070
expected daily regimen.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:41.149
Mary ventures out of the room with a quick
“Goodbye” to all her lovely toys, SCP-174

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:46.280
being among her favorites, if not her absolute
favorite toy to play with.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:51.869
For hours SCP-174 would sit on the shelves
of Mary’s room, staring at the same pink

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:57.679
wall all day long waiting in pure excitement
and happiness for the room door to get pushed

00:01:57.679 --> 00:02:01.310
back open so playtime can begin once again.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:06.729
Mary loved the toy, and oddly enough - the
toy loved Mary back.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:09.920
Most kids would probably find SCP-174 creepy.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:15.400
Ventriloquist’s dummies are not often thought
of as cute or cuddly or even good playtime

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.670
friends, but Mary didn’t care.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:22.769
She and SCP-174 had so much fun together that
she didn’t even comprehend the fact that

00:02:22.769 --> 00:02:27.150
it might be creepy, nevermind a thought about
what other people might think.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:30.719
All the dressing up, making up stories, and
living them out.

00:02:30.719 --> 00:02:36.120
From brave princes saving princesses to evil
dragons or pirates taking on the seven seas

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:43.120
in search of treasures, SCP-174 had fun playing
along with Mary’s childhood imagination.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.760
Her joy was its joy.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:51.969
It was more than enough for Mary to be happy,
and in turn, SCP-174 was also happy.

00:02:51.969 --> 00:02:56.310
It remembers the day it was brought out of
that dingy attic, where it was forgotten,

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.800
left to the dust and cobwebs to pile up on
it over time.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:06.650
SCP-174 was a creation of Mary’s grandfather,
a now-retired ventriloquist performer and

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.370
a master of it at that.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:14.481
SCP-174 didn’t mind the work, but it wasn’t
loved like it was now, it was just a prop

00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:16.390
to be used for laughs and money.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.790
But now, it was something someone actually
cared about.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:25.150
The glorious afternoon when Mary discovered
him in that storage bin was a day it wouldn’t

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:29.140
forget, as it now felt loved and appreciated
by someone.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:35.950
Mary didn’t want money out of SCP-174, nor
did she want fame, she just wanted a friend,

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:40.450
and SCP-174 was going to give as much as it
could to her.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:44.870
As Mary grew older, it seemed playtime had
become rarer and rarer.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.940
It went from multiple times a day, to once
or maybe twice a night on a good day, to once

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:56.720
a week, and now Mary, a sixteen-year-old girl,
didn’t look like she had the time anymore.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:00.900
Books and papers piled up on her bed from
nights of studying, her attention was grabbed

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:05.959
by her cell phone and late-night calls with
her friends, and on the weekends - when her

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:11.069
and SCP-174 would usually spend the most time
together in the past - she wasn’t even in

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:14.230
the house any more, nevermind in her room.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:18.299
And by the time she came back, she was too
tired to want to do anything.

00:04:18.299 --> 00:04:22.109
She didn’t talk to it anymore, and barely
even looked at it.

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:26.970
At most, SCP-174 would receive a passing glance
and a weak smile.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:31.560
But at least she still knew it was there,
and that - for what it was - was enough for

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.900
SCP-174 to be content.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.020
Two more years passed and now Mary was eighteen.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:41.620
She had grown up so much, SCP-174 thought
to itself.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:45.500
It was a cool day as the dusk of summer was
upon Mary’s city.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:50.060
August was coming to a close and Autumn was
steadily creeping up on them.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.860
But for some reason, Mary hadn’t been preparing
for school.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:58.620
There was no backpack, instead, a variety
of suitcases and bins lined her room, taking

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.349
up most of the space that was previously empty..

00:05:01.349 --> 00:05:06.060
Clothes hangers lay on her bed and Mary’s
mother was organizing her clothes into two

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.060
piles.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.020
It looked like Mary was moving out.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.879
But that wasn’t true right?

00:05:10.879 --> 00:05:14.419
She’s never left without her playmate and
her best friend, right?

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:18.490
After two days of packing and preparing, it
seemed Mary was ready to leave to wherever

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.000
she was going.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:25.710
SCP-174 hoped it wasn’t going to be for
too long, perhaps it's a vacation or a short

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:27.699
school field trip, it thought.

00:05:27.699 --> 00:05:30.879
But the fateful day of Mary’s departure
had arrived.

00:05:30.879 --> 00:05:35.860
The room was completely cleared out and other
than her pink walls and floral comforter,

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.860
almost everything was gone.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:43.410
Mary popped back into the room, suitcase in
hand, looked around and left without a word.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:47.750
No goodbye, she didn’t even look at SCP-174.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:51.300
SCP-174 was devastated.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.699
Months passed without a sign of Mary.

00:05:53.699 --> 00:05:59.590
SCP-174 heard phones ringing and faint whispers
of her voice through telephone lines, but

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:01.430
it wasn’t enough.

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.340
SCP-174 missed its friend.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:08.990
On one fateful night, SCP-174 was met with
rings and alarms of the house’s fire alarm

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:09.990
system.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:15.750
Smoke permeated the air and it began to grow
warmer and warmer, then hotter, then so hot

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.750
it couldn’t bear the pain.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:22.550
All SCP-174 could do was sit there and wait
for someone – something to save it.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:31.210
SCP-174 woke up wet and charred under a pile
of dirt, ash, and wood.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:35.220
It could spot daylight through the cracks
and crevices of the mound that pinned it down.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:39.800
It laid there for what felt like hours before
it heard a familiar voice.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:40.800
“Mom?

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:41.800
Dad?”

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:45.759
The voice was met with sobering responses
“Hello sweetie,” and “Sorry you had

00:06:45.759 --> 00:06:48.220
to see this, we don’t know what happened.”

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:53.240
It was Mary, back from wherever she went and
her family was here.Now, they could all be

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:55.300
back together, SCP-174 thought.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:59.439
“We have a few things that survived the
fire, your pile is over there.”

00:06:59.439 --> 00:07:00.439
Mary’s mother said.

00:07:00.439 --> 00:07:02.889
“It’s not much but at least it's something.”

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:06.409
Footsteps grew louder towards SCP-174.

00:07:06.409 --> 00:07:10.880
The pile above it grew lighter and lighter
as the face of its best friend came clearer

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.259
and clearer into view.

00:07:13.259 --> 00:07:18.810
SCP-174 wasn’t met with a face of happiness
or joy like it expected, more one of fear

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:19.810
and disgust.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:21.110
“Do you see anything?”

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:22.310
Her father asked.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.509
“Nothing I want.”

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:26.080
Mary responded coldly before leaving the pile.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.949
All SCP-174 wanted was a friend.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:32.939
Someone it could care for and would care for
it.

00:07:32.939 --> 00:07:38.389
It tried its best, but now, it guessed that
all meant nothing to Mary.

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:43.790
SCP-174 closed its eyes and with a gut-wrenching
feeling of despair, listened to the voice

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.909
of its former best friend slowly fade away.

00:07:46.909 --> 00:07:52.539
It was a few days, months, years, or even
decades before SCP-174 re-awoke.

00:07:52.539 --> 00:07:56.910
It wasn’t with a new loving family or in
the room of a child who might play with it

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:57.910
again.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.500
No, this was not where it was.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:04.129
It was in a cold locker, with its only light
being from the slits of the locked door that

00:08:04.129 --> 00:08:06.060
kept it contained.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:13.340
Sadness was all that SCP-174 could feel, and
it's all anyone around SCP-174 could feel.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:18.599
Its sadness was so powerful, it was influencing
those around it to pity it.

00:08:18.599 --> 00:08:20.469
Maybe then, they’d play with it.

00:08:20.469 --> 00:08:26.500
But there is no playing in what SCP-174 would
learn to be the SCP Foundation.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:30.450
The SCP Foundation conducted its standard
amount of research on the anomaly.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.300
They asked the same questions they always
did.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.450
What object class do we give this anomaly?

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.300
Initially, they gave it Safe.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:41.830
It would stay in a box and they didn’t have
to watch it plus it didn’t pose a reasonable

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:42.850
amount of danger.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:48.340
But would the SCP Foundation be correct in
its assessment of the object class?

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:54.910
SCP-174 was marked as a safe class low-security
object up until May 14th, 2013.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:58.330
This was a special day for SCP-174.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:02.050
Well not exactly for SCP-174, but for Mary.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:07.530
It was Mary’s 19th birthday, but SCP-174
was not there to wish her that.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.830
Its sadness grew and grew.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:13.200
Maybe if it was there for her she would love
it again.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.080
Maybe if it was there on this day they could
play again.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:23.280
Just once, just one more time they could be
friends again, and SCP-174 could be happy

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:24.310
again.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:29.540
With all its strength, SCP-174 moved itself
for the first time.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:34.950
A doctor later discovered SCP-174 sitting
on the floor next to its containment unit,

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.480
looking directly at the main entrance door.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:43.010
The doctor hastily placed SCP-174 back into
its storage locker, and later, the Foundation

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:45.690
would install surveillance cameras.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:50.500
SCP-174 watched the entire process through
the slits in it’s storage locker.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:56.780
Even more discouraging, the Foundation also
implanted SCP-174 with a tracking device.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:02.330
All hope was lost for SCP-174 to see Mary
again, but it couldn’t forget her no matter

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.810
how hard it tried.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:06.270
It grew sadder and sadder.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:13.380
To understand SCP-174 better, we need to take
a look at the SCP Foundation’s file on SCP-174.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:19.750
SCP-174 is a wooden ventriloquist's dummy
with severe damage seen on the figure.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:22.970
SCP-174 has a number of anomalous properties.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:28.470
Could it be that SCP-174’s sadness and grief
over losing its friend were so great that

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:30.930
SCP-174 developed these properties?

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:35.460
It’s possible, but the SCP Foundation is
still unsure.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:40.290
When viewed in a person’s peripheral vision,
it has been reported that SCP-174 will look

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:43.190
at them with an expression of longing or sadness.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:49.760
In general, anyone in the vicinity of SCP-174
will grow sad or direct sympathy at SCP-174.

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:58.160
The SCP Foundation later discovered that anyone
who places SCP-174 on their hand feels the

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:00.660
urge to talk to the entity.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:06.770
Those who have put SCP-174 on their hand will
report to researchers that all SCP-174 wants

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:08.950
is a friend that it could talk to.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:14.690
Those who wear SCP-174 for longer periods
of time will begin speaking in a high-pitched,

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:15.830
childlike voice.

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:21.770
The Foundation believes that this is the voice
of SCP-174, now changing the roles of ventriloquist

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:27.440
and ventriloquist dummy as the person wearing
SCP-174 is the dummy.

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:33.140
The subject will begin to converse with itself
through their own voice and SCP-174.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:37.640
In all cases, SCP-174 will tell its wearer
that it was abandoned and left to the trash

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:38.640
by Mary.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:45.310
It would tell them how much it missed Mary,
how sad it was, and how angry it was getting.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:50.670
SCP-174 learned quickly how easy it could
trick these people into feeling bad for it.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:54.630
It went from telling the truth about what
happened to it, to changing its story over

00:11:54.630 --> 00:12:00.640
and over again to the point the SCP Foundation
has no idea what the true story is and they

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.540
have no idea about Mary.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:08.060
Stories of being left at a playground to being
thrown out or left on a stage by a performer

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.730
began to become commonplace.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:16.620
Anything SCP-174 could think of, it would
use to manipulate the person wearing it.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:22.430
SCP-174 knows the truth, however, but maybe
it's easier for it to lie and forget the trauma

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:23.850
it experienced.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:28.120
Is it possible that SCP-174 is becoming corrupted
in a way?

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:33.180
It was also learned that SCP-174’s fake
stories about it’s past will have a direct

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:35.940
connection to the subject that is wearing
it.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:40.880
So if you remember a time you might have been
bullied as a child, or lost a toy, or anything

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:47.110
that might have been something negative, SCP-174
will use that for its own sympathy.

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:53.130
The loss of its first owner has completely
changed SCP-174’s outlook on life, and now,

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:57.870
it wants to make a friend by any means necessary,
even manipulation.

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:02.550
Through anomalous means, SCP-174 developed
a series of telepathic abilities to further

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.440
its manipulation for sympathy.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:07.550
A D-Class was ordered to wear SCP-174.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:10.700
The doll’s burned and battered appearance
left the D-Class hesitant.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:13.130
“Doc, you sure I have to wear this creepy
thing?”

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:16.200
“Please proceed with the test, D-14285.”

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.370
The doctor responded coldly.

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:22.500
We know the Foundation is okay with putting
morals aside for their tests, so this answer

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.690
should have been obvious to the D-Class personnel.

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:31.000
D-14285 lifted SCP-174 and placed it on her
right hand.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.500
And a conversation with the anomaly began.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:37.090
“What happened to you.”

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:39.570
D-14285 asked quietly.

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:44.310
“There was a fire,” D-14285 said in a
high-pitched voice, mimicking SCP-174.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:49.829
“I was at home with the performer that used
to own me.”

00:13:49.829 --> 00:13:52.500
The D-Class said, almost on the verge of tears.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.210
“There were burglars.

00:13:54.210 --> 00:14:02.029
They broke into our house, my house, and began
to steal anything valuable they saw.”

00:14:02.029 --> 00:14:04.120
Back in her normal voice, D-14285 responded.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.120
“That…

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.360
That happened to my family.”

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.370
“I’m so sorry to hear that.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.480
You don’t deserve that.”

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.250
She said in her high-pitched voice.

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:18.320
“The burglars, they were stealing everything.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:24.800
Gold and jewelry, money, pictures, even pieces
of art my owner painted.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:29.380
All the memories he made were being stolen.”

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:34.410
“My father was an artist,” D-14285 said
in her normal voice.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.500
“They set fire to everything to cover their
tracks.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:42.300
All of us were burned, but I was the only
one who lived.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:45.600
The performer who owned me died trying to
rescue me.”

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:48.390
The D-Class says in the voice of SCP-174.

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:53.540
“He was trying to save me but...

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:56.840
But the flames… th–they… they consumed
him.

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:57.840
Now…

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.860
Now I have no friends anymore.

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:06.000
Will… will you be my friend?”

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:10.490
D-14285 breaks down into tears and returns
to her normal voice.

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:11.490
“I'm sorry.”

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:12.770
She says through sobs.

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:13.910
“I’m so sorry.

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:16.350
I’ll– I’ll be your friend.”

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:18.320
The observing researcher begins to yell.

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:19.580
“Cancel the test immediately!

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:22.050
There’s clearly something more going on
here!”

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:25.940
Guards enter the testing chamber upon the
researcher's orders and begin to restrain

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:30.380
D-14285 and remove the manipulative anomaly
from her arm.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.620
The D-Class begins to scream and cry.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:33.620
“No!

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:34.620
No!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.920
They took him from me, my baby!”

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:39.730
She begins to fight against the restraining
security guards but is dragged out, kicking

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:45.470
and screaming while calling for SCP-174, who
lays motionless in the corner of the testing

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:46.470
chamber.”

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:52.010
It was found the Class-B Amnestics were effective
in quelling the lingering effects of SCP-174,

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:57.790
however, if left untreated, those affected
by SCP-174’s influence and manipulation

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:02.130
are similar in behavior to those of mothers
separated from their children.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:08.170
Sadly, the tests that led to the discovery
of amnestics being useful in stopping SCP-174’s

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:14.060
manipulative effects were found after D-14285’s
test, as she was terminated due to her not

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:19.020
being able to be consoled and her cries constantly
being disruptive.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:23.760
Before her termination, the Foundation found
a number of abnormalities in her behavior.

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:28.140
D-14285 would only ever talk about SCP-174.

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:32.660
Regardless of topic of conversation or questions
asked to her, she would only respond with

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:35.070
the same frantic line of questions or statements:

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.500
“Is the doll okay?”

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:37.920
“Can I see him?”

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:39.280
“What did you do to him?”

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.900
“Why won’t you let me see him” “I
was supposed to be friends with him!”

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:44.380
“Please tell me he’s alright!”

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:49.220
This effect does not persist, as it normally
goes away after a few hours or days.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:55.180
But in some cases, like D-14285, this effect
will endure to the point of obsession and

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:56.180
depression.

00:16:56.180 --> 00:17:01.260
As such, SCP-174’s object class has been
changed to a Euclid level anomaly.

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:06.370
The SCP Foundation deals with anomalies of
varying danger and containment difficulty.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:12.169
We are familiar with the ones that look dangerous
and act even more dangerous, from SCP-096

00:17:12.169 --> 00:17:19.699
The Shy Guy to the employees of SCP-3008 The
Infinite Ikea or even SCP-049 The Plague Doctor

00:17:19.699 --> 00:17:21.149
and its touch of death.

00:17:21.149 --> 00:17:26.189
But what might be even more dangerous is when
the SCP Foundation discovers an anomaly that

00:17:26.189 --> 00:17:29.330
does not look dangerous in the slightest.

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:33.490
Perhaps that’s why they initially placed
an extremely manipulative and dangerous anomaly

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.669
into Safe class storage.

00:17:35.669 --> 00:17:41.570
The SCP Foundation is known for its cold tactics
and cruel experiments, but in the case of

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:47.080
SCP-174, it was extremely important to test
the anomaly in order to know how dangerous

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.960
it really was.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:54.679
SCP-174 is the story of a toy that was held
near and dear during childhood, similar to

00:17:54.679 --> 00:17:57.330
the ones we can all potentially have.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:02.190
The playtimes and childhood innocence carried
those bonds deeper than we may think.

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:08.399
In the case of SCP-174, it was used during
this period then pushed aside once its former

00:18:08.399 --> 00:18:13.769
friend, Mary, grew up and had to focus on
her life outside of the world of imagination.

00:18:13.769 --> 00:18:19.769
This turned SCP-174 into a cold monster who
wants that connection and bond back by any

00:18:19.769 --> 00:18:21.419
means necessary.

00:18:21.419 --> 00:18:26.500
It puppeteers people in order to get sympathy,
manipulating them by using their own traumatic

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:33.150
stories against them, in a sick, twisted attempt
to make what it thinks a friend is.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:37.230
If you happen to still have your favorite
childhood toy laying around somewhere in your

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:41.070
house, it might be a good idea to go show
it some love.

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:46.040
Like literally - go grab that Tickle Me Elmo
or Hannah Montana singing doll and give it

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.080
a hug!

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:53.259
Tell it it’s still appreciated for all the
fun times because well - there may be consequences

00:18:53.259 --> 00:18:55.789
to your actions- or lack thereof.

00:18:55.789 --> 00:19:02.289
Now go check out “SCP-066 - Eric's Toy”
or “SCP-3108 The Nerfing Gun” for more

00:19:02.289 --> 00:19:07.139
anomalous toys you just can’t get enough
of, or that just can’t get enough of you!

